  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its second run: 13 witnesses pass, the rule uses 27 names and composes no other rule, and it declares 1 narrowing of my own.\n\n**Gate runs (2 of 6 used):**\n1. `WITNESS_FAIL`. I ran it too early, before writing the scenes. The rule already built and passed the static checks; the only failures were the empty skeleton scenes, which had no track 1.\n2. `OK`, with the 6 planned witnesses plus `branch_3` to `branch_9`. Those extra branches give each remaining exception its own scene: the queue behind traffic, the stop sign, the yield sign, the red signal, the railway lights, the railway gate and the police officer.\n\nSeparately, I tried one shell command other than the gate. It was denied automatically and nothing ran; it wasn't needed.\n\n**How the rule reads:** for each restricted-parking curb zone the subject occupies, the subject must not be halted unless one of four exceptions holds:\n- **(a)** another road user is ahead of it in the same lane within the queue gap;\n- **(b)** a stop sign, yield sign, signal, railway signal or gate, or police officer requiring a halt governs the lane it is in;\n- **(c)** the zone sign's conditions hold for the subject;\n- **(d)** it is a temporary passenger stop: not a truck or trailer, not parked, a door open at some point of this halt, and no qualifying vehicle waiting just outside the zone at any point of the halt so far.\n\n**Choices the node left open:**\n- **Signal colours (declared narrowing on s1).** I read \"a red or yellow indication\" as steady red or yellow, circular or arrow, plus flashing red. Flashing yellow is not read as an order to halt.\n- **\"Gate not up.\"** I wrote this as a gate that is lowering, down or raising, so a railway device with no gate doesn't count. I didn't declare it as a narrowing because it matches the node's own words, \"a gate not up\"; the rule file's header explains it.\n\n**Witness notes:** in the short-stop scenes the car is moving at the start, so the look-backs have a decided starting point. In `blind` and `branch_1` it is also moving at the end, so `blind` is unknown only because the doors are unobserved.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/fsw/portfolios/av/projects/av_alpamayo_reasoning/users/wcong/WorldModelSpec/.worktrees/full221-v2/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent`:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_510.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_510.lean`\n- `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484B_510/task_result.md`",
